{
  "what": "Exact word pins of the diff_opt=2 metric trajectories (3 steps, km_opt 2/4, open and periodic, dry and moist) and of the two legacy checkpoint resumes, re-measured on the 2.8.8 release line. The 2.8.7 pins (diff2-merged-baseline.npz, diff2-merged-legacy.npz) and their word attribution (diff2-merged-attribution.json) are kept unchanged as the record of what 2.8.7 ran.",
  "why": "The 2.8.8 Group A integration deliberately moved the default dycore arithmetic: the diffusion units (smag2d, diffusion, diff_opt1, diff6, diff6_seam) compile with IEEE options and run WRF's diffusion order by default (54 intake), and verify-base4 moved the acoustic, diagnostics and bigstep arithmetic. The 2.8.7 tree reproduces the 2.8.7 pins exactly (0 moved words at 70e2d5c6f on this card); reverting only the 54 default diffusion route at the 2.8.8 tip does not restore them (30,947 words still move), so the move is the combined integration, not one lane. The individual intake commits do not import on their own, so a per-intake attribution is not measurable. The diffusion operators themselves are graded word for word against compiled WRF by tools/diffusion_default_check.py (km4, km2, km3, diff1, diff6, w_damp: 0 different words on this card in the default and strict arms).",
